Priya K.: opened PR https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/802 — adds a small troubleshooting section for HSM PKCS#11 setups and a recommended systemd unit drop-in that gracefully reloads client TLS certs used by the pkcs11-tls tunnel. need: a concise Go SDK snippet showing TLS client config for mTLS + SAN pinning, and a short socat test for piping PKCS11 over TLS for docs.
Jon Chen: nice. can you paste the systemd drop-in you have in mind? want to make sure it doesn't break rpm/deb upgrades.
Priya K.: draft drop-in: ```ini
[Unit]
Description=Reload pkcs11-tls cert on rotation
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/pkcs11-cert-reload --socket /var/run/pkcs11-tls.sock
RemainAfterExit=yes

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```
purpose: small helper that signals long-running tunnel process to reload certs post-rotation. we link to our cert-rotation playbook.
Lucas H.: add a note: for systemd, use `ExecStartPre` to validate cert parse, avoid leaving socket dangling. also, if the tunnel runs as non-root, show `RuntimeDirectory=pkcs11-tls` and `RuntimeDirectoryMode=0750`.
Maya (tech writer): can you keep that to 3-4 lines and i'll fold into the 'cert rotation' subsection. also need the socat test and the Go snippet. i'll soften language for operators.
Priya K.: socat test (single-line) to verify TLS connectivity to HSM proxy: `socat - OPENSSL:127.0.0.1:8443,verify=0,cert=client.pem,key=client.key`  this demonstrates a simple TLS connection that echos stdin to the tunnel. add a warning: do not use `verify=0` in prod, it's just for quick local checks.
Jon Chen: Go snippet (minimal) that shows mTLS + server name validation + pin allowed SANs: ```go
package main
import (
  "crypto/tls"
  "crypto/x509"
  "fmt"
  "net/http"
)
func main() {
  certPool := x509.NewCertPool()
  // load CA... (omitted)
  cfg := &tls.Config{
    RootCAs: certPool,
    MinVersion: tls.VersionTLS12,
    // ensure the server certificate contains an expected SAN
    VerifyPeerCertificate: func(rawCerts [][]byte, verifiedChains [][]*x509.Certificate) error {
      cert, _ := x509.ParseCertificate(rawCerts[0])
      for _, dns := range cert.DNSNames {
        if dns == "hsm-proxy.internal" {
          return nil
        }
      }
      return fmt.Errorf("unexpected SANs: %v", cert.DNSNames)
    },
  }
  tr := &http.Transport{TLSClientConfig: cfg}
  client := &http.Client{Transport: tr}
  resp, err := client.Get("https://hsm-proxy.internal/health")
  if err != nil { panic(err) }
  defer resp.Body.Close()
  fmt.Println("status", resp.StatusCode)
}
```
Maya (tech writer): great, concise. i'll replace the comment with a one-liner note "load CA bundle from /etc/redwood/ca.pem" and add a short caution about VerifyPeerCertificate complexity.
